          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Comments: — Bixa atlantica can be distinguished from B. orellana, the best represented species of the genus in herbaria, and the only other one that also occurs in the Atlantic Forest domain, due to the absence of nectaries in the pedicel apex (rarely inconspicuous) near the calyx (vs. conspicuous in B. orellana), the leaf base rounded truncate or rarely slightly cordate (vs. cordate or truncate in B. orellana), the habit of trees up to 20 m, rarely treelets or shrubs (vs. shrubs or treelets 5 –",
